WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:08.240
Choppy trade continues as the Nifty gives up&nbsp;
gains to hover around the lowest point of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:15.200
session below the 25700 mark. Broader indices&nbsp;
however stay in the positive territory. Metals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:28.720
and PSU banks remain resilient while IT, auto&nbsp;
and real estate stocks stay under pressure.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:32.880
ICICI Lombard delivered strong premium&nbsp;
growth and market share gains in Q3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.400
but profitability took a hit due to&nbsp;
higher claims costs and one-time labor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:47.440
code impact. ICICI credential life meanwhile&nbsp;
saw brokerages turn constructive on margins.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.200
Inforce is expected to report a modest&nbsp;
sequential revenue growth and largely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.680
stable margins with constant currency&nbsp;
growth slowing despite currency tailwinds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:04.800
Investors will track commentary on tech spending,&nbsp;
pricing pressure, and enterprise AI adoption.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:12.160
December WPI data edged up to 0.83% reversing&nbsp;
the deflationary print of a third of a percent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.920
lower in November. The data came in well&nbsp;
above street expectations. The rebound is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:24.240
being largely attributed to base effects and&nbsp;
a pickup in food and global commodity prices.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.720
Indian rail railways may seek up to a&nbsp;
10% hike in capital outlay this budget&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.600
with a sharp focus on safety, capacity&nbsp;
expansion and private participation. Big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.840
ticket priorities include funding for&nbsp;
the Kawatch train protection system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:51.600
new rail tracks and state&nbsp;
and station redevelopment.

